# CMM Routers — local bearer tokens only.
# Host is fixed to 127.0.0.1 by schema; port lives in config/shared.json.
# Copy nothing secret into git: this file holds only the token variable names.
#
# CMM_ROUTER_TOKEN authenticates the CMMChat profile, which is permanently
# CHAT_ONLY on every provider (no tools, no shell, no edits). No request
# metadata can ever elevate it.
CMM_ROUTER_TOKEN=
#
# CMM_CODE_ROUTER_TOKEN is the canonical Code Router profile bearer. Requests
# presenting it authenticate the Code Router profile, which may use tools ONLY
# on providers whose structured upstream round-trip is proven (CHAT_AND_TOOLS).
# This is a profile credential, not a client identity: Qoder, Hermes, Codex and
# generic OpenAI-compatible harnesses all authenticate the same profile.
CMM_CODE_ROUTER_TOKEN=
#
# CMM_QODER_TOKEN is the legacy compatibility alias for the Code Router profile:
# it authenticates the SAME profile as CMM_CODE_ROUTER_TOKEN. Retained so
# existing installations keep working; it is no longer a distinct role. When
# neither Code Router bearer is set there is no Code Router profile and every
# authenticated client is CMMChat (CHAT_ONLY).
CMM_QODER_TOKEN=
#
# Cavoti is an explicit PAYG route. It remains disabled in shared config and
# also requires a separate machine-local spend acknowledgement before the
# Router will register it. This example intentionally contains no secret value.
CAVOTI_API_KEY=
